// forge_reserve_launcher.rue -- Forge V14. Testnet research only; unaudited.
//
// The coin a reserve is born from. It creates exactly one coin -- the reserve, at the
// puzzle hash it is told, for its whole amount, hinted with the pool's launcher id -- and
// makes a COIN announcement saying so.
//
// Why it exists (spec 1.3, review R-1): `register` used to take each reserve's parent id
// from its solution, and nothing in the registration bundle proved the reserve had been
// funded. A registration naming parents that created nothing succeeded, and the slot it
// took could never be spent by anyone. Now `register` is given each reserve's GRANDPARENT
// and derives the parent itself:
//
//     P_i = coinid(grandparent_i, RESERVE_LAUNCHER_HASH, reserves[i])
//
// then asserts this puzzle's announcement from P_i. A coin id commits to its puzzle hash,
// so the only coin that can make that announcement is one running this puzzle -- and this
// puzzle does nothing but create the reserve. Both halves at once: the id fixes WHICH coin,
// the puzzle fixes WHAT it did.
//
// For a CAT reserve this puzzle is the inner of a CAT coin: the CAT layer wraps the created
// puzzle hash and passes the announcement through, so `register` derives P_i with
// cat_puzzle_hash(asset_id, RESERVE_LAUNCHER_HASH) and asserts the same message.
//
// solution: created_puzzle_hash, amount, launcher_id

import forge_action_common::reserve_launcher_message;

fn main(created_puzzle_hash: Bytes32, amount: Int, launcher_id: Bytes32) -> List<Condition> {
    assert amount > 0;
    [
        // the whole coin becomes the reserve: nothing else is created here
        AssertMyAmount { amount: amount },
        CreateCoin {
            puzzle_hash: created_puzzle_hash,
            amount: amount,
            memos: Memos { value: [launcher_id] },
        },
        CreateCoinAnnouncement { message: reserve_launcher_message(created_puzzle_hash, amount, launcher_id) },
    ]
}
